{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Evan, and thanks Marisol for structuring this. Let me go through the four areas. On practical constraints: our current separate structures — separate organizers, mailing lists, and volunteer rosters — mean we'll need a clear plan for how we consolidate or coordinate those resources without losing either group's identity or reach. On past working experiences: I have to be honest here. I personally observed exactly two heated exchanges between the two group leads about event ownership. Based on that, I believe the first six shared meetings require an independent facilitator to help us establish a productive working rhythm. I didn't file a formal complaint because I didn't want to escalate the disagreement, but I do think it's important to surface this now so we can build the right support into the structure. On process requirements: I'd like to see the independent facilitation I just mentioned built into the governance structure for at least the first six meetings, along with clear decision-making protocols. On operating commitments: I'm willing to commit to transparent scheduling, shared documentation, and regular check-ins to make sure both groups stay aligned. I also want to make sure we're respecting Evan's scheduling constraint he just raised."}
```

